# GhostDriver — run checklist for our next session

We will continue with the unchecked items below. The first goal is live CARLA
video between the two networks; leave driving controls stopped until video works.
Secret values belong only in the ignored .env files, not in this checklist.

## Done

- [x] Dashboard token configured (confirmed by you).
- [x] Sender token configured (confirmed by you).
- [x] Cloudflare Tunnel client, cloudflared, installed (confirmed by you).
- [x] Remote-video code and separate setup guides added.
- [x] Local validation passed: 11 backend tests, 2 browser tests, 4 Python tests,
      and the frontend build. Tests used a demo sender / CARLA API stub;
      real CARLA and the two-network connection still need testing.

## Your laptop — next steps

- [ ] Configure an external TURN service in backend/.env:
      TURN_URL, TURN_USERNAME, TURN_PASSWORD. Keep the STUN_URL setting too.
      Both peers receive these settings from the authenticated backend.
      Leaving all TURN fields empty permits a STUN-only trial, but connections
      across different networks may fail.
- [ ] Check that actual .env files and credentials are excluded from the GitHub
      changes. Commit .env.example templates only.
- [ ] Commit and push the updated project so your friend can get the same code.
- [ ] From the Ghostdriver folder, start the website and backend:

      npm run dev

      If dependencies are missing, run npm run setup first. Use Node 22.12+.
- [ ] Open http://localhost:5173, enter the dashboard token, and click
      Connect backend. Keep the app terminal running.
- [ ] In a second terminal, start the tunnel:

      cloudflared tunnel --url http://127.0.0.1:4000

- [ ] Share the printed HTTPS tunnel address with your friend, and share the
      sender token privately. Do not share the dashboard token or put tokens
      in the URL. Keep cloudflared running.

## Your friend's GPU computer

- [ ] Clone the GitHub repository, or pull the latest changes.
- [ ] Confirm the installed CARLA simulator version and choose a Python version
      compatible with its matching CARLA Python wheel and bridge dependencies.
- [ ] Create and activate a Python virtual environment. From the project root
      on Linux:

      python3 -m venv carla-service/.venv
      source carla-service/.venv/bin/activate
      python -m pip install -r carla-service/requirements.txt

      On Windows PowerShell, use py instead of python3 to create the environment,
      then activate with carla-service/.venv/Scripts/Activate.ps1.
- [ ] Install the CARLA Python client matching the simulator version exactly.
      Use the matching wheel's actual path with python -m pip install.
- [ ] Copy carla-service/.env.example to carla-service/.env and fill in:

      BACKEND_URL=<the public HTTPS tunnel address>
      SENDER_TOKEN=<the privately shared sender token>

      No separate TURN settings are needed on this computer.
- [ ] Start CARLA with rendering enabled and an asynchronous world. Keep its
      ports private; do not forward or tunnel ports 2000–2002.
- [ ] With the virtual environment active, start the bridge from the project root:

      python carla-service/bridge.py --host 127.0.0.1 --port 2000

      Keep CARLA and the bridge running. Your friend does not need to start
      React, Node, or cloudflared.

## Together — verify video first

- [ ] On the laptop, confirm Sender connected, then CARLA ready.
- [ ] Click Connect beside the sender, then Start stream.
- [ ] Confirm actual CARLA footage, nonzero received FPS, packet-loss readings,
      and the Direct / TURN relay route indicator.
- [ ] Stop video, enable Test TURN only, and start again. Confirm received
      video and TURN relay. Then stop and disable the option for normal use.
- [ ] Test connection loss/recovery. Video must clear when frames stop, and
      controls must remain stopped after recovery. After a signaling reconnect,
      select the sender and start video again.
- [ ] Only after video works, deliberately test Resume controls, W/A/S/D,
      emergency stop, and focus-loss braking with your friend watching CARLA.

